<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Ba Vi by Motorbike: Choosing a Bike for the Trip</h1>
<p>The Ba Vi trip does not need a special motorcycle, it needs a well-matched ordinary one. The route west of Hanoi asks for a machine that is comfortable at city pace, relaxed on the open plain, patient on a long climb and honest on the way home, and the Hanoi rental fleet contains several verified categories that can do all four. This guide walks through what the ride actually demands of a machine and how to choose between the categories with your own comfort as the deciding vote.</p>
<p>Every machine in this comparison can be rented from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk hands over western-trip bikes daily and answers the choice questions this guide raises. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, read the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/hanoi-to-ba-vi-motorbike-route/">Ba Vi route guide</a>, see the fleet and the terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">What The Ride Asks Of A Machine</a></li>
